# Fix Session Persistence and Login Rerouting

The user is experiencing issues where they are rerouted to the login page after logging in. This is caused by the backend's in-memory session store ([session_store.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py)) losing state during server reloads or due to unsynchronized in-memory state in multi-worker environments. Although it attempts to persist to [sessions.json](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/data/sessions.json), the loading/saving logic is fragile and prone to race conditions or stale data.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [session_store.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py)
- Improve the [load_sessions](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py#13-24) and [save_sessions](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py#25-33) functions to be more robust.
- Ensure that [load_sessions](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py#13-24) is called before every session check if possible, or at least ensure the in-memory map is synchronized with the file.
- Add logging to track when sessions are loaded and saved.

#### [MODIFY] [auth.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/auth.py)
- Explicitly call [load_sessions()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py#13-24) before accessing the [sessions](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/session_store.py#13-24) dictionary in the [logout](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/auth.py#207-218) and other relevant endpoints to ensure the latest data is used.

### Verification Plan

#### Automated Tests
- Run [backend/prepare_test_user.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/prepare_test_user.py) to ensure local DB has a user.
- Create a script `backend/test_session_persistence.py` that:
    1. Calls the login API.
    2. Verifies [sessions.json](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/data/sessions.json) is updated.
    3. Manually re-initializes the session store and checks if the session is still valid.

#### Manual Verification
- Log in through the browser.
- Verify that the session persists across page refreshes.
- Manually restart the backend server and verify that the session is still valid (not redirected to /login).
